# Keyword ownership

Avoid cannibalization. Each major intent has one primary URL. Source of truth: `src/data/keywordOwnership.ts`.

| URL | Primary keyword | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | War Thunder cheats | Homepage. May support War Thunder hacks. |
| `/war-thunder-cheats/` | War Thunder cheats | Long-form. Must be distinct from `/` — not a duplicate homepage. |
| `/war-thunder-hacks/` | War Thunder hacks | Do not make this the homepage’s primary H1. |
| `/features/esp/` | War Thunder ESP | |
| `/features/aimbot/` | War Thunder aimbot | |
| `/features/radar/` | War Thunder radar | |
| `/features/wallhack/` | War Thunder wallhack | |

## Rules

- Before creating any new URL, define its search intent in `keywordOwnership.ts`
- Do not ship a page whose title/H1 compete with another owner for the same primary query
- Internal links: send ESP/aimbot/radar/wallhack queries to their feature URLs once those pages exist; until then, homepage section anchors are fine
- Homepage may mention secondary terms naturally; it must not be written as four feature landing pages
- `/war-thunder-cheats/` is not live until it has a unique angle vs `/`
